# Bulletproof Errors And Performance

## Errors

- Handle API failures in `api-client` (toast or centralized mapping, refresh once on 401, clear session if refresh fails).
- Put an error boundary around the app **and** around heavy feature routes so one crash does not take down the SPA.
- Data routes still own loading, empty, error, and forbidden UI. Error boundaries catch render/unexpected failures, not expected `403`/`404` JSON.
- Do not log tokens, cookies, or personal data in error payloads.

## Performance

- Lazy-load heavy routes with `React.lazy` + `Suspense`. Split at the route boundary, not every component.
- Colocate state to cut extra rerenders. Use `children` to isolate expensive subtrees from parent state.
- Do not wrap everything in `useMemo`/`useCallback`. Memoize when a measured rerender or an unstable dependency needs it.
- Keep query `staleTime` and retries in `src/lib/query-client.ts`; override per hook only when the screen needs polling or no-retry 4xx.
